    <string name="profile_detail_download_tooltip">Download is traffic arriving from the network to your device</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_jitter">Jitter</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_jitter_tooltip">Jitter adds random variation on top of base latency. Physically, it models unstable queueing, interference, and uneven packet timing on mobile or congested links</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_latency">Latency</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_latency_tooltip">Latency adds a fixed delay to packets in both directions. Physically, it models long-distance routes, radio scheduling delay, or slow upstream links</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_loss">Loss</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_loss_tooltip">Loss drops a percentage of packets before they are delivered. Physically, it models weak signal, interference, congestion, or damaged links where packets never arrive</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_stalls">Stalls</string>
    <string name="profile_detail_stalls_tooltip">Stalls pause traffic completely for short bursts and then resume it. Physically, it models dead zones, radio handovers, elevator rides, and brief network freezes. Each stall lasts for a random 70–100% of the configured duration so it feels less robotic</string>
